---
/**
 * A caveat set apart from the body text, not an alert.
 *
 * What these hold are honest admissions of limits: a sample too small, a thing
 * that never ran in production, a problem still open. So the register is quiet
 * — a tinted ground at full body measure, no icon, no accent bar, no colour
 * that reads as danger. An `aside` because the content is tangential to the
 * argument, not a warning about it.
 *
 * Styling lives in public/assets/article.css under `.prose .callout`, not in a
 * scoped style block here: the rules have to reach the markdown the slot
 * renders, which Astro's component scoping deliberately does not.
 *
 * Available to every MDX post without an import — see the `components` prop in
 * src/pages/articles/[...slug].astro.
 */
---

<aside class="callout"><slot /></aside>
